  "narrative": "No discovery assessments are due. The strongest dataset structure remains the near-additive dominant predictors: feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 are associated with higher outcome_001, while feature_037=1 is associated with lower outcome_001. The principal secondary signal is feature_063. The reverse feature_063 association (feature_063=1 associated with lower outcome_001, i.e. stronger composite dependency) is accepted in several contexts but remains ambiguous as a global average because H166 has a signed point estimate above threshold but a lower bound just below threshold. Existing evidence indicates that this reverse association is strongest when feature_038 is high and feature_018 is low, with weaker or reversed patterns among high feature_018 contexts and especially extreme high feature_018 interactions. I therefore propose comparisons that complete and sharpen the feature_018-by-feature_038 decomposition around feature_063, while separating context-specific modification from any average feature_063 effect. The exact dominant-zero low-feature_018/low-feature_038 contrast tests whether the reverse association survives in the clean background when the strongest modification by feature_038 is absent. If strong, it would support a feature_018-driven reverse effect independent of high feature_038; if null, it would support context dependence on high feature_038. The exact dominant-zero high-feature_018/high-feature_038 reverse contrast completes the clean 2x2 decomposition and tests whether feature_038 can restore the reverse association even among median-high feature_018 records. The global low-feature_018/upper-quartile-feature_038 and high-feature_018/high-feature_038 direct contrasts refine the median-split findings using more extreme thresholds. The upper-quartile feature_018/high-feature_038 positive-direction contrast is motivated by accepted interactions H191 and H192, which imply that at sufficiently high feature_018 the raw feature_063 contrast may become positive, i.e. feature_063=1 associated with higher outcome_001 and weaker dependency. The reversed feature_063-by-feature_018 interaction in high feature_038 directly tests the raw positive interaction implied by the rejected negative-direction H189. Finally, the middle feature_038 band tests whether a reverse feature_063 association exists outside the extreme feature_038 quartiles, helping distinguish an average effect from an effect confined to feature_038 extremes. For direction -1 direct feature_063 claims, a positive signed estimate means feature_063=1 associated with lower outcome_001; for direction +1 direct claims, a positive signed estimate means feature_063=1 associated with higher outcome_001. These remain observational Welch comparisons in the supplied dataset with opaque predictor labels, overlapping subgroups, and no assigned biological roles; they do not establish causality, mechanism, or generalizability beyond the supplied and independent validation samples.",
  "research_notes": "Core accepted dataset structure: feature_010=1 -> outcome_001 about +0.83 (discovery) and +0.82 (validation); feature_002=1 -> about +0.81/+0.85; feature_037=1 -> lower outcome_001 by about 0.80 (accepted reverse-direction claim). Pairwise dominant-predictor interactions mostly null, including feature_037-by-feature_002. Secondary signal: feature_063=1 associated with lower outcome_001 in many contexts, commonly around 0.25-0.35 units and larger in feature_038-high contexts; feature_038 modification of feature_063 is validated globally (H177), in dominant-zero background (H187), and among feature_010=0 (H188). Low-feature_018 reverse feature_063 contrasts are accepted, especially when feature_038 is high; high-feature_018 direct reverse contrasts are null, weak, or borderline, while extreme high-feature_018 interaction claims accepted active but small/borderline. H166 global reverse feature_063 remains unresolved/active and is the top validation target if analysis policy allows: signed estimate +0.239, lower +0.145, just below threshold. If validation supports it, feature_063 may be characterized as an average dataset association; if not, context-specific modifier is preferred. Existing H202 already tests global low-feature_018 x low-feature_038 direct reverse and is active; do not duplicate. New registered refinements prioritize clean 2x2 mapping: dominant-zero low-low, dominant-zero high-high, global high-low, low-high upper quartile, extreme upper-feature_018 positive direct, reversed high-feature_038 feature_018 interaction, and middle-band feature_038. Interpret all with direction carefully: for feature_063 direction -1, positive signed estimates = lower outcome_001/stronger dependency; direction +1 positive = higher outcome_001/weaker dependency. Avoid overclaiming from overlapping subgroup analyses or exact 20-cell results."
